:"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009026","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7922e5b45feacc79a10d95c454a19bb42a44ca3c8b90184221a2a4bf37560de4","compact":"50d0a0dda17e1affb003bfd9074ef95001634f80408dcebca47999769b352c5a","nasal":"ae4d696e92a3f42260d2bbfaf5da8bb0cbb80eb6b05da3826cd02db773bcae0c"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-27","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":27,"english":"And at one place, a female, borne down by the force of sleep, forcibly possessing herself of another's cloth, and wrapping herself there with, went to the bed of that one, and was indulging in sleep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.8,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009027","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"20744ee3cddf4609cbb30c2a48859b1cc16357e93ade1d158c592ed7f7e56faa","compact":"00a95bf28c55ebf14e4db5b1469b8545cad6124a3c4f0d223d50e685d15f1f8d","nasal":"00a95bf28c55ebf14e4db5b1469b8545cad6124a3c4f0d223d50e685d15f1f8d"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-28","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":28,"english":"And with their breath, their variegated wreaths and the cloth on their persons were stirring gently, as if with a mild-blowing breeze.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.803,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009028","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"b8a15fd6b77200a96ff5657d63c06298605813f0576bbb66490e6b68d391414a","compact":"2ec597164aa490ed0bad8a2723a1bc24203f6e00d6b4a5c0abd5444a85c77c9e","nasal":"1d6d21d9deeb357f73b04e460407b1db8437d85cb56427e51ce8925e19284356"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-29","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":29,"english":"Laden with the odours of cool sandal, and of sweet-tasting Sidhu; and of diverse wreaths and flowers, and with perfumes of various kinds, and entranced with (the aroma) of sandals suitable for use after ablution, and of dhupas, the air, impregnated with excellent scent, was there breathing around the car Puşpaka.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.86,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009029","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"03c6527fe0a73055d8c2a6e4add015aace9f3f4286fc92cef9d6fa505fab5b63","compact":"9c4aae2a7555e4601cd3795dd2ba7c2df97b7e4651f12dfe0fdd13af636e8625","nasal":"f528381852876dcf515f5edb5f3df648ed3f21407d5a764d0017908a192788c3"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-30","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":30,"english":"Laden with the odours of cool sandal, and of sweet-tasting Sidhu; and of diverse wreaths and flowers, and with perfumes of various kinds, and entranced with (the aroma) of sandals suitable for use after ablution, and of dhupas, the air, impregnated with excellent scent, was there breathing around the car Puşpaka. And in the residence of the Rākşas, there were some wenches sable, yet exceedingly witching; and some were dark-hued; and the frames of some were of a golden brilliance.","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.551,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-22","DUTT-5-11-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009030","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0f052cf82c0bc95905b03300a4644b4d907e7084425e835e7e30654f796e48ba","compact":"ebd3332e3dfcbd029e7a3695768655a036b9f4ae8b8c141ef1a4513a56e5c254","nasal":"98dd3915295c3806a969d9251c399813611b4262c824e56f16a2d0bb9c873d77"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-31","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":31,"english":"And in the residence of the Rākşas, there were some wenches sable, yet exceedingly witching; and some were dark-hued; and the frames of some were of a golden brilliance.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.9,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-23"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009031","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"74f8da40717d4c76b9dae1d0be72f5836d1f447d941dbea4a1c529e67e60bcff","compact":"fbeae0bebe2fe24844dd3004b4c296030f685b13a9d3ee8bdfd5d5c3efffac40","nasal":"e0eab643ff3d535c6b024f168a6fccc13d1bad0517c89fdc3055d94ed0a94f0e"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-32","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":32,"english":"Their beauty, in consequence of their coming under the governance of sleep, and their being bereft of their senses by Madana, resembled that of lotuses in a sleep.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.909,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-24"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009032","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"27f222572f871880bba632d90756164cf685197bba21e42b49ac31cffe7a1e1f","compact":"e95df89427f4dbac1b145286f0e7b915560847fd98f39a795e849a5bc90a72a8","nasal":"cce0cf59c0fb2085a607c02edfd3a1e671c01e4e9890ea074b635489a87b36e4"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-33","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":33,"english":"Thus that highly energetic monkey saw everything thoroughly in the inner apartment of Ravana, but he saw not Janaka's daughter.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.843,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-25"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009033","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"188ba89187a5f0a7e5f191b7f60e10d0aca6219ea0ff0b70e449cd2ff6faf730","compact":"7a92defc44bc3f6146f44edd4bafb206f3cb8ef0d57e232e747570a642781b2a","nasal":"24080eb154a4394c95801caae9b64ccc4b7d8c029bd7cfbb4624738cd0a57f49"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-34","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":34,"english":"Seeing those females, that mighty monkey, apprehending loss of righteousness, was seized with an exceeding great fear.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.806,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-26"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009034","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4ed456af68f08e37cf55a3a7d5776e7e0cb6f76183f1a0445f09bc1d2c57435d","compact":"74b38a0352a3211f8976850287cb2277ef6b3ec4411f0315a7ade23f2d930b36","nasal":"e948d02e058d485e43328efa3996f7b764a773fa2e24fb47d065b74f27ee4573"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-35","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":35,"english":"Beholding a female, who is the religiously wedded wife of another, while she is asleep, verily cause loss of righteousness. *And therefore presumably incapable of taking care of herself.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-27"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009035","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"ffe71ddc0965889201b723eee425bbeaaf0a2dc8ac137b8721cf9514bc7801c6","compact":"05ae42f33c4ad265d6999599d961fc9cfcc5ab8a56c6efdd18425c487c6c4610","nasal":"05ae42f33c4ad265d6999599d961fc9cfcc5ab8a56c6efdd18425c487c6c4610"}},{"id":"VRCE-5-9-36","kanda":5,"kandaId":"sundara","sarga":9,"verse":36,"english":"My sight surely never seek other's wives; but I have beheld this one that has ravished another's spouse.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.839,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-5-11-28"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"5009036","sanskritFile":"Ram05.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"50eff5d14c5ff387759db5270d64